        "module": "https://cardstack.com/base/file-formats/metadata-fields",
        "name": "ExifMetadataField"
      },
      "readMe": "# EXIF Metadata\n\n## Summary\nThe EXIF pair: how the photo was taken and where.\n\n## Shape\nDeliberately thin — two contained fields, `capture` (`CameraCaptureField`) and `location`\n(`GeoLocationField`). The split matters because the two halves have different privacy weight and\ndifferent availability: a studio photo has capture data and no location, and a location may survive\nstripping that removes body and lens. Consumed by `RasterImageDef.exif`, so every raster format\ninherits the same shape.\n\n## Example\n```ts\nimport { ExifMetadataField } from 'https://cardstack.com/base/file-formats/metadata-fields';\n\n@field metadata = contains(ExifMetadataField);\n```\n",
      "containedExamples": [
        {
          "capture": {
            "make": "Apple",
            "cameraModel": "iPhone 15 Pro",
            "focalLength": {
              "value": 24,
              "unit": "mm"
            },
            "aperture": {
              "value": 1.78,
              "unit": "f/"
            },
            "exposureTime": {
              "value": 0.0166,
              "unit": "s"
            },
            "iso": 80,
            "flash": {
              "code": "16",
              "scheme": "exif-flash"
            },
            "orientation": {
              "code": "1",
              "scheme": "exif-orientation"
            }
          },
          "location": {
            "latitude": 48.8584,
            "longitude": 2.2945,
            "placeName": "Champ de Mars",
            "city": "Paris",
            "country": "France",
            "source": {
              "code": "ios-photos",
              "scheme": "geo-source"
            }
          }
        }
